WEBVTT

00:00:01.387 --> 00:00:03.518
Michael Jordan.

00:00:03.578 --> 00:00:08.520
People in every country know that name.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.141
They know his face.

00:00:11.201 --> 00:00:16.152
They know his number, 23.

00:00:16.213 --> 00:00:19.914
He is tall and strong.

00:00:19.974 --> 00:00:23.095
He has a lot of money.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:26.506
He is very famous.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:30.739
And he can fly.

00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:35.722
Michael Jordan is a basketball player.

00:00:35.782 --> 00:00:41.814
He played for 13 years for the Chicago Bulls.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:46.695
Many people understand basketball.

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:51.647
A lot of people love basketball.

00:00:51.707 --> 00:00:57.088
But Michael Jordan lives basketball.

00:00:57.148 --> 00:01:01.864
Every game is important to him.

00:01:01.924 --> 00:01:05.460
But where did he come from?

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:11.274
How did he win six NBA championships?

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:15.976
When did he start to fly?

00:01:16.036 --> 00:01:19.018
Early days.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:27.575
Michael's story starts on February 17, 1963, in Brooklyn, New York.

00:01:27.635 --> 00:01:38.765
The family moves to Wilmington, North Carolina later in 1963.

00:01:38.825 --> 00:01:45.170
Michael is the son of Dolores and James Jordan.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:51.283
He comes from a happy home with a lot of love.

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:59.986
One old friend says, the Jordan's door was always open.

00:02:00.046 --> 00:02:06.366
Mr. and Mrs. Jordan talked to us and listened to us.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:13.338
There was always a basketball game in the backyard.

00:02:13.398 --> 00:02:20.010
Young Michael's best friend is his brother, Larry.

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:27.004
Larry teaches his little brother a lot of things about basketball.

00:02:27.064 --> 00:02:51.702
Mr. Jordan builds a big basketball court for his sons and their friends This is Michael's first basketball school Today Michael says We played basketball games every day on Saturdays.

00:02:51.762 --> 00:02:59.727
We were on our court all day rain No problem.

00:02:59.786 --> 00:03:04.129
We played basketball.

00:03:04.189 --> 00:03:12.404
For a long time, Larry is the best basketball player in the Jordan family.

00:03:12.464 --> 00:03:16.288
Baseball is Michael's game.

00:03:16.348 --> 00:03:20.010
He is strong and quick.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:24.244
He always wants to win.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:33.352
The Jordan children have jobs at home, but Michael doesn't like working.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:38.686
His brothers and sisters have money for things.

00:03:38.746 --> 00:03:44.940
Michael doesn't have any money because he doesn't work.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:51.946
The only jobs in his life are baseball and basketball.

00:03:52.006 --> 00:04:06.434
Basketball at school From 12 to 15 years old, Michael plays baseball, basketball, and football at school.

00:04:06.494 --> 00:04:10.466
He is short for a basketball player.

00:04:10.526 --> 00:04:13.308
He is only 1.75 meters, 5 feet, 9 inches.

00:04:13.328 --> 00:04:21.860
Mr. and Mrs. Jordan are under 1.75 meters.

00:04:21.919 --> 00:04:32.193
Michael isn't going to be very tall.

00:04:32.253 --> 00:04:39.227
In 1978, Michael starts his three years at Laney High School.

00:04:39.286 --> 00:04:46.030
His teachers say now, Michael was a good student.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:51.980
He was quiet, but he had a lot of friends.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:59.132
Michael starts basketball at Laney on the A team.

00:04:59.192 --> 00:05:02.405
Larry is on the A team too.

00:05:02.425 --> 00:05:04.627
He has number 45.

00:05:04.647 --> 00:05:15.604
Michael asks for number 23 because 45 divided by 2 equals 22 and a half.

00:05:15.664 --> 00:05:24.837
But Michael doesn't stay on the A-Team.

00:05:24.897 --> 00:05:29.558
The coach moves him to the B-Team.

00:05:29.618 --> 00:05:32.409
Michael is angry.

00:05:32.469 --> 00:05:35.980
He wants to be on the best team.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:42.912
He plays basketball every morning, afternoon and evening.

00:05:42.972 --> 00:05:47.302
Sometimes he doesn't go to school.

00:05:47.362 --> 00:05:50.689
His father talks to him.

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:58.267
Basketball is important, but school is important too.

00:05:58.327 --> 00:06:02.958
Michael goes back to school.

00:06:03.018 --> 00:06:07.920
It is the summer of 1979.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:15.232
Mr. Jordan remembers, Michael wanted to be tall.

00:06:15.292 --> 00:06:19.634
He wanted to be on the 18.

00:06:19.694 --> 00:06:29.265
Suddenly, He was 1.91 meters, 6 feet, 3 inches tall.

00:06:29.325 --> 00:06:35.050
In September, Michael plays on the A-Team.

00:06:35.109 --> 00:06:40.844
He is the star of basketball at Laney.

00:06:40.904 --> 00:06:47.279
The A-Team games start at 7.30 in the evening.

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:54.088
Before 5 o'clock, The people of Wilmington are waiting at the court.

00:06:54.148 --> 00:06:57.860
They want to see Michael.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:03.924
Laney wins its first championship that year.

00:07:03.984 --> 00:07:06.875
College life.

00:07:06.935 --> 00:07:12.989
Now Michael thinks about basketball after Laney.

00:07:13.048 --> 00:07:16.546
A lot of colleges want him.

00:07:16.606 --> 00:07:26.530
Michael likes the University of North Carolina UNC in Chapel Hill.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:32.134
He likes the basketball coach Dean Smith.

00:07:32.194 --> 00:07:41.292
Michael goes to UNC in September 1981 with his sister Roslyn.

00:07:41.352 --> 00:07:48.380
She is a very good student and she starts college early.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:55.450
Dean Smith teaches Michael a lot of things about basketball.

00:07:55.510 --> 00:08:03.626
Remember, every player on the team is important, he says.

00:08:03.686 --> 00:08:07.540
Michael works on his game.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:15.084
He is on the first team in his first year at UNC.

00:08:15.144 --> 00:08:23.048
Michael is the best new player in college basketball in 1981-22.

00:08:23.108 --> 00:08:35.677
The UNC team, the TAR heels, get to the 1982 college basketball championships.

00:08:35.736 --> 00:08:47.488
They are going to play the Georgetown Hoyas There are 61,000 people in New Orleans for the big game.

00:08:47.548 --> 00:08:53.561
It is Tar Heels 61, Hoyas 62.

00:08:53.621 --> 00:08:59.144
There is only a little time in the game now.

00:08:59.204 --> 00:09:06.930
Dean Smith says to his players, get the ball to Michael.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:10.876
Michael has the ball.

00:09:10.936 --> 00:09:14.492
the Hoyas run at him.

00:09:14.552 --> 00:09:18.562
But Michael doesn't look at the players.

00:09:18.622 --> 00:09:22.113
He looks at the basket.

00:09:22.174 --> 00:09:25.334
He takes a long shot.

00:09:25.394 --> 00:09:29.056
The ball is in the basket.

00:09:29.116 --> 00:09:35.837
UNC wins its first college championship.

00:09:35.897 --> 00:09:44.368
The story of the shot is in the newspapers and on TV.

00:09:44.428 --> 00:09:47.270
Michael is famous.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:55.152
His photo and the shot are on the Chapel Hill telephone book in 1982.

00:09:55.172 --> 00:10:01.118
The NBA, 1984 to 93.

00:10:01.178 --> 00:10:12.796
Every year, the teams in the NBA look for good new players.

00:10:12.856 --> 00:10:22.281
After three important and happy years at UNC, Michael Jordan thinks about the NBA.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:31.436
But Dolores Jordan says to her son, Finish your four years at UNC.

00:10:31.496 --> 00:10:34.926
It's very important.

00:10:34.986 --> 00:10:47.588
Michael says, I'm going to go to the NBA, but I'm going to finish my college work too.

00:10:47.648 --> 00:10:52.172
Michael finishes his work at UNC in 1986.

00:10:52.232 --> 00:10:56.452
His mother is very happy.

00:10:56.512 --> 00:11:07.818
In June of 1984, the NBA teams are looking for tall players.

00:11:07.878 --> 00:11:14.622
Michael is 1.98 meters, 66 inches.

00:11:14.682 --> 00:11:19.806
He isn't very tall for the NBA.

00:11:19.866 --> 00:11:31.828
The Houston Rockets take Hakim Alajuan 2.08 meters, 6 feet, 10 inches.

00:11:31.888 --> 00:11:43.058
The Portland Trailblazers take Sam Bowie, 2.16 meters, 7 feet, 1 inch.

00:11:43.118 --> 00:11:49.284
Then at number 3, Jordan hears his name.

00:11:49.344 --> 00:11:53.073
The Chicago Bulls want him.

00:11:53.133 --> 00:11:58.461
The Bulls aren't a good team in 1984.

00:11:58.521 --> 00:12:04.133
They win only 27 of 82 games.

00:12:04.193 --> 00:12:12.145
But they give Michael $6 million for 7 years.

00:12:12.205 --> 00:12:20.063
The Bulls always say to their players, you play for us now.

00:12:20.123 --> 00:12:24.031
No basketball on your vacations.

00:12:24.091 --> 00:12:27.864
This is your job.

00:12:27.924 --> 00:12:33.926
But Michael wants to play with his friends and with Larry.

00:12:33.986 --> 00:12:37.348
The bulls want Michael.

00:12:37.408 --> 00:12:49.748
They say, OK Michael, you can play for us and you can play for the love of the game too.

00:12:49.808 --> 00:12:57.954
In July of 1984, Michael catches an airplane to Los Angeles.

00:12:58.014 --> 00:13:02.596
He is on the 1984 U.S.

00:13:02.656 --> 00:13:05.308
Olympic basketball team.

00:13:05.368 --> 00:13:10.880
The best college players in the country are on the team.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:18.060
They win their games and the Olympic award for basketball.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:22.948
Michael gives his award to his mother.

00:13:23.008 --> 00:13:30.812
He plays again and wins in the 1988 Olympic Games.

00:13:30.873 --> 00:13:38.626
After the 1984 Olympic Games, Michael starts his job with the Bulls.

00:13:38.686 --> 00:13:46.319
In the NBA, he can be a big star on the basketball court.

00:13:46.379 --> 00:13:52.482
Nike makes shoes for basketball players.

00:13:52.542 --> 00:13:59.428
People from Nike say, this new star can fly.

00:13:59.488 --> 00:14:03.410
He's going to be very famous.

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:07.844
Nike makes a shoe for Michael.

00:14:07.904 --> 00:14:12.307
Its name is Air Jordan.

00:14:12.367 --> 00:14:19.512
Now Michael plays and people say, Can he fly?

00:14:19.572 --> 00:14:23.044
Or is it the shoes?

00:14:23.104 --> 00:14:28.848
People buy a lot of Air Jordan shoes.

00:14:28.908 --> 00:14:36.134
In two years, Nike makes $130 million from them.

00:14:36.194 --> 00:14:41.147
Michael makes a lot of money from them too.

00:14:41.207 --> 00:14:45.180
Michael loves the NBA.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:48.216
His game is strong.

00:14:48.276 --> 00:14:51.611
people like watching him.

00:14:51.671 --> 00:14:57.956
But life away from the basketball court is often difficult.

00:14:58.016 --> 00:15:01.740
People always want to talk to him.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.474
Michael can't walk down the street.

00:15:05.534 --> 00:15:10.198
He can't go to a store or to a movie.

00:15:10.257 --> 00:15:14.010
People want to be his friend.

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:20.618
In 1985, Michael meets Juanita Vanoy.

00:15:20.678 --> 00:15:25.851
She is smart and beautiful and interesting.

00:15:25.911 --> 00:15:30.674
But she doesn't know about basketball.

00:15:30.734 --> 00:15:36.058
She likes Michael because he is a good person.

00:15:36.118 --> 00:15:41.162
They want the same things in life.

00:15:41.222 --> 00:15:56.589
From 1984 to 1987, Michael wins a lot of awards in the NBA, but he wants to win the NBA championship.

00:15:56.649 --> 00:16:03.031
The newspapers ask, is Jordan a team player?

00:16:03.091 --> 00:16:08.342
Can the Bulls win the championship?

00:16:08.402 --> 00:16:20.206
From 1987 to 1990, The Bulls get some new players and a new coach, Bill Jackson.

00:16:20.266 --> 00:16:26.581
The Bulls start to build a championship team.

00:16:26.641 --> 00:16:34.738
In December 1988, there is a very happy story in the newspapers.

00:16:34.798 --> 00:16:39.281
Michael and Juanita have their first son.

00:16:39.342 --> 00:16:43.674
His name is Jeffrey.

00:16:43.734 --> 00:16:48.136
Bulls are very good.

00:16:48.196 --> 00:16:53.108
They win 61 of 82 games.

00:16:53.168 --> 00:17:00.102
The Bulls and the Los Angeles Lakers are in the championship games.

00:17:00.162 --> 00:17:06.355
The Bulls win the championship in five games.

00:17:06.416 --> 00:17:12.289
Michael says, we're a strong team.

00:17:12.348 --> 00:17:17.498
After seven years, We did it.

00:17:17.559 --> 00:17:22.921
Now, no team can stop the Bulls.

00:17:22.982 --> 00:17:26.184
They win the championship in 1992 and in 1993.

00:17:26.204 --> 00:17:28.826
The newspapers say, Michael Jordan is the best.

00:17:28.846 --> 00:17:35.932
He can win every game.

00:17:35.992 --> 00:17:48.471
Michael has many awards and three championships in three years.

00:17:48.532 --> 00:17:58.519
He and Juanita now have two sons, Jeffrey and Marcus, and one daughter, Jasmine.

00:17:58.579 --> 00:18:06.544
After the championships in 1993, Michael goes home with his family.

00:18:06.604 --> 00:18:10.524
He is strong and happy.

00:18:10.584 --> 00:18:14.571
A new baseball star?

00:18:14.631 --> 00:18:21.573
Things are good for the Jordan family in the summer of 1993.

00:18:21.633 --> 00:18:28.164
But then, one day, Michael's father visits some friends.

00:18:28.224 --> 00:18:32.576
That evening, he doesn't come home.

00:18:32.636 --> 00:18:36.947
The police find him in a river.

00:18:37.007 --> 00:18:46.024
Two 18-year-old boys killed him for his car and his money.

00:18:46.085 --> 00:18:54.010
Michael loved his father very much, and he can't understand this.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:19:00.384
Why did these boys kill a good man?

00:19:00.444 --> 00:19:07.416
On October 6, 1993, Michael and Juanita are on TV.

00:19:07.476 --> 00:19:15.507
Michael says, life is very short.

00:19:15.567 --> 00:19:20.308
I want to have time with my family.

00:19:20.368 --> 00:19:24.790
Michael retires from basketball.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:28.791
The Bulls retire his number, 23.

00:19:28.851 --> 00:19:48.292
Early in 1994, Michael starts a new job in baseball Michael and a lot of young players try for a place on the Chicago White Sox baseball team.

00:19:48.352 --> 00:19:51.222
Michael can run well.

00:19:51.282 --> 00:19:57.824
He can catch well, but he can't hit a baseball very well.

00:19:57.884 --> 00:20:06.714
The newspapers say, Mike, please come back to basketball.

00:20:06.774 --> 00:20:11.044
But Michael likes playing baseball.

00:20:11.105 --> 00:20:15.186
In baseball, he isn't a star.

00:20:15.246 --> 00:20:18.878
Michael's number is 45.

00:20:18.938 --> 00:20:21.668
Larry's old number.

00:20:21.728 --> 00:20:30.352
But in August 1994, there are problems in baseball about money.

00:20:30.412 --> 00:20:34.064
The players stop the games.

00:20:34.124 --> 00:20:38.288
They don't play for a long time.

00:20:38.348 --> 00:20:42.672
Michael is 31 years old.

00:20:42.732 --> 00:20:47.014
He can't wait for baseball.

00:20:47.074 --> 00:21:04.034
The NBA 1995-8 On March 8, 1995, the Chicago Bulls Office gives a story to the newspapers.

00:21:04.095 --> 00:21:08.385
It is a short story from Michael Jordan.

00:21:08.445 --> 00:21:13.316
It says, I'm back.

00:21:13.376 --> 00:21:19.640
Chicago is a very happy town that night.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:28.976
Michael is happy with the Bulls again and with his old friends and his coach Phil Jackson.

00:21:29.037 --> 00:21:34.832
The team works well and starts to win again.

00:21:34.892 --> 00:21:41.249
Michael is number 45 in the championship games.

00:21:41.309 --> 00:21:45.572
The Bulls aren't doing very well.

00:21:45.632 --> 00:21:57.512
Some players say number 45 is okay, but number 23 was a star.

00:21:57.572 --> 00:22:01.286
This makes Michael angry.

00:22:01.346 --> 00:22:05.170
He goes back to number 23.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:11.394
Now, the players remember, he's back.

00:22:11.454 --> 00:22:17.336
The Bulls don't win the championship in 1995.

00:22:17.396 --> 00:22:21.258
In the summer, Michael has some time.

00:22:21.278 --> 00:22:26.980
He makes a movie, Space Jam.

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:29.832
Children love it.

00:22:29.892 --> 00:22:33.638
It makes a lot of money.

00:22:33.698 --> 00:22:49.736
The Bulls start 1995-6 with a new player, Dennis Rodman, and some old players, Scotty Pippen and Michael Jordan.

00:22:49.796 --> 00:22:55.317
The Bulls are the best team in the NBA again.

00:22:55.377 --> 00:23:00.054
And Michael Jordan is their star.

00:23:00.114 --> 00:23:11.666
The Bulls win the NBA Championship in 1996, 1997 and 1998.

00:23:11.726 --> 00:23:23.286
Michael Jordan has six NBA Championship Awards and he has basketball awards in every room in his house.

00:23:23.346 --> 00:23:27.490
But there are always problems in life.

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:32.444
The Chicago Bulls office wants a new coach.

00:23:32.504 --> 00:23:37.768
But Michael Jordan likes playing for Phil Jackson.

00:23:37.828 --> 00:23:43.981
The NBA players are unhappy about their money too.

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:49.944
They start the games late in 1998.

00:23:50.004 --> 00:23:55.856
Then Michael and Juanita are on TV again.

00:23:55.916 --> 00:24:04.180
Michael retires from basketball on January 13, 1999.

00:24:04.240 --> 00:24:11.164
He has good times and bad times in his first 36 years.

00:24:11.224 --> 00:24:19.080
But we remember Michael Jordan because he can fly.

00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:25.520
Michael has a lot of money from his life in basketball.

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:33.866
In 2000, he buys an NBA team, the Washington Wizards.

00:24:33.926 --> 00:24:37.558
They aren't a good team.

00:24:37.618 --> 00:24:42.328
Michael Jordan isn't a player this time.

00:24:42.388 --> 00:24:45.909
It is his team.

00:24:45.969 --> 00:24:51.280
This is an interesting time for basketball.

00:24:51.340 --> 00:24:56.213
Is Michael Jordan's team going to fly.

